# Stochastic Process

In [Probability Theory](probability.dj), a stochastic process is a mathematical object usually defined as a family of random variables. 
It is used to represent the evolution of some random value, or system, over time.

## Common Examples

One of the most famous and widely applied examples of a stochastic process is the [Markov Chain](markov_chain.dj). 
Another foundational example is the Wiener process (or Brownian motion).

::: note
Stochastic processes are widely used as mathematical models of systems and phenomena that appear to vary in a random manner.
:::